WEBVTT

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.970
Today we're having sukiyaki.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.170
Wow.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.680
Meat was really cheap today.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:47.890
What's wrong, Kana?

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.690
Why aren't you acting all stupid and happy?

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.950
All right! I'm digging in!

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.010
What's this all of a sudden?!

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.440
Don't just take all the meat!

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.080
Besides, that's my meat!

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:14.800
Now, now. There's still plenty of meat left, don't fight!

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:34.450
How fearsome.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:42.530
I've suddenly become afraid of myself.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.540
Can't you hear me out for a bit?

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:53.090
What is it?

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.620
It seems that I've acquired a supernatural power.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:02.580
It's true!

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.940
Yesterday was fried shrimps. Today was sukiyaki.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.970
What we're going to have for dinner the next day appears in my dream.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:11.890
These are prophetic dreams!

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:18.580
You don't believe me?

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:22.550
No... but all you did was mention things that have already occurred.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.740
Telling people that those events were foreseen is a bit...

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:30.320
Then, if I can predict what we'll have for tomorrow's dinner, will you believe me?

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.410
Fine, if your prediction is right then I'll believe you.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.750
Then I'll dream of it tonight.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.170
My cold body is all warmed up.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.830
You should dip in too, Chiaki!

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.330
What are you eating?

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:15.870
Kana! Kana!

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:20.300
I'm busy right now.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.380
If you need something, please leave a message after the tone.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.770
It's going to be a girl!

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.630
Right next to you! Right next to the convenience store!

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:35.230
Kana, this is all your fault.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:42.570
What was that red stick thing?

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:43.730
Carrot?

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:52.160
How come Mako-chan was...

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.080
Oh well.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:58.590
But I wonder how Makoto is doing?

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:04.580
Even though he keeps saying he hates wearing girl's clothing, he seems to be having fun doing it.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.750
Is it going to be all right if I leave him alone?

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.510
I'll ask him directly next time.

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:22.940
So how did your prophetic dream turn out?

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:25.600
It was peculiar.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:29.040
I can sort of remember it, but...

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.030
You can't say it?

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.040
No, it's not that I can't say it, but...

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:36.620
I knew this would happen.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.550
What prophetic dream nonsense.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:39.780
Hold it, Chiaki!

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:41.150
What now?

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.250
I have something important to say!

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.990
For instance, Uchida hates eating rice cakes...

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:50.670
What are you saying all of a sudden? Uchida does eat rice cakes.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.790
Just listen to me!

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.900
Let's pretend that Uchida hates eating rice cakes.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:59.430
In the process of continuously eating the rice cakes that she hates, she slowly becomes fond of it.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.690
That's possible, right?

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:05.500
Stop it, she'll just hate rice cakes even more.

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:06.400
Is that so?

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:10.930
But depending on how she eats it, it's plausible.

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:16.500
People can change under the influence of people around them.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:18.280
Whether it's good or bad.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.240
Like the one who kept saying she can predict the future.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:25.230
If others around her pay her no heed, sooner or later she'll stop mentioning it.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.130
These are two different matters!

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:34.410
Prophetic dream, eh?

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:38.300
She really surprised me when she said that suddenly.

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:41.400
Somehow I feel like we're missing something today.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:44.430
I guess Hosaka-senpai is off today.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:45.820
Eh? What?

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:47.060
Oh, nothing!

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.940
What is it?

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:50.590
Really, it's nothing!

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:51.920
Minami-san.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:55.110
Yes. What is it, sensei?

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:58.010
Can you come by the guidance office?

00:06:58.010 --> 00:06:59.880
You mean now?

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.560
What I want to say is, Minami-san...

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:07.190
You've probably heard of our student exchange program, right?

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:07.870
Yes.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:13.710
I hope that you, with your excellent grades, can help represent our school overseas.

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:16.550
Eh? But I...

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:19.400
I know you may have your circumstances, but this is a great chance.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:27.110
Go and explore this vast world while you're still young, and meet all sorts of people.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.950
You'll likely benefit a lot from this.

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:48.650
Don't just go ignoring a friend who's in distress.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:51.410
S–So you were in distress...

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:55.550
What can I do to precisely recall my dreams?

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.150
Give me some good ideas!

00:07:58.150 --> 00:07:59.930
Hmm, let's see...

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:04.180
How about jotting it down the moment you wake up?

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:06.600
Impossible! Like I could do something like that!

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:08.640
I shouldn't have asked you.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.310
Then don't ask me...

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:14.730
So that's what happened.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:16.900
That's so like Kana-chan.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:18.350
You think so?

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:21.250
I think she's just talking in her dreams.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:25.340
What?

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.210
No, nothing.

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:35.090
We'll go throw out the trash.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.620
You guys use this time to finish cleaning.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:38.210
Yes!

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:41.920
Chiaki has changed.

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:43.280
Changed?

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:44.260
How so?

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.110
She seems to be more chatty lately.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:51.660
Really? She tends to stay silent whenever I talk to her.

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.740
You could say she ignores me.

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:58.650
Chiaki didn't really like to get involved with others in the past.

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:00.280
You've changed too, Makoto-kun.

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.320
You're infatuated with girl's clothes now!

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:03.770
That's not true!

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:04.920
I wonder about that.

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:08.350
That's only because Kana keeps on asking me to do so.

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:11.420
I'm just showing the servicing spirit that I've inherited from my father.

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:13.620
It's true!

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:18.680
I'm going over to Chiaki's place to do homework today. Are you jealous?

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.500
Did Kana-san say anything about letting Mako-chan come along?

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.340
I wonder...

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:27.210
What did you say about homework?

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.890
What? You're coming too?

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:34.230
Umm... can I come along too?

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:36.690
I'm back.

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:38.980
Hurry up and come in.

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:39.980
Sorry for disturbing.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:40.240
Sorry for disturbing.
Sorry for disturbing.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.460
Sorry for disturbing.

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:45.200
Hey, I'm back.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.420
Sorry for disturbing!

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.540
Oh! Yoshino! Uchida too!

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:53.210
I–It's been a while!

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:54.920
Who are you?

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:58.050
This guy? He's not a very interesting character, even if he tried to be.

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:00.990
Sorry for disturbing.

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.310
Huh? Makoto?

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.720
I've gotten permission from Chiaki!

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:06.600
I can visit as myself in full glory today!

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:08.100
Oh?

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:10.850
I don't have to be ordered around by you anymore.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:15.560
Those actions I took, the masculine spirit inherited from my mother would never approve of them!

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.180
I didn't give you permission!

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.690
This is my home!

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:31.020
I know you've just arrived here, but get out now!

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:32.890
N-No way...

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:34.090
We don't need you here!

00:10:48.990 --> 00:10:50.170
Makoto-kun!

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:55.450
Kana-chan told me to give this to you.

00:10:58.770 --> 00:11:00.110
Sorry for disturbing.

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:02.440
Oh! It's Mako-chan.

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:04.740
As expected, you're quite energetic.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:07.900
You think so? I don't quite get it either!

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:24.260
Vessel No. 1 has suffered heavy damage! Our troops are being annihilated!

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:26.450
All right, send out our new unit.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.470
We have to protect this area at all costs!

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:32.260
Preparation for lift off complete.
Bridge, on standby until order is given.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:33.280
Hey, Kana!
Preparation for lift off complete.
Bridge, on standby until order is given.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:34.020
Roger. Transmitting data. Send reinforcement for Vessel No. 1.
Hey, Kana!

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:34.030
I said Kana!
Roger. Transmitting data. Send reinforcement for Vessel No. 1.
Hey, Kana!

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:36.120
Roger. Transmitting data. Send reinforcement for Vessel No. 1.
I said Kana!

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:37.440
Hey, Kana!
Roger. Transmitting data. Send reinforcement for Vessel No. 1.

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:40.820
Is my disguise perfect?

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:40.830
Huh?
Is my disguise perfect?

00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:41.240
Huh?

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:45.080
I'm asking you whether my disguise is perfect or not.

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:47.170
Well, I suppose so.

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:49.990
Chiaki hasn't discovered it.

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:52.890
Uchida knows my true identity.

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:56.930
Then what about Yoshino?
Do you think Yoshino will find out?

00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:59.010
She'll probably find out.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:01.350
What are you worrying about?

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:03.480
If you're worried about being exposed then you can just stop, you know.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:04.720
B–But...

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:09.180
You sound as though I forced you into wearing girls clothing.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:10.680
But you've always had the freedom of choice.

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:14.500
You have wings that allow you to fly freely in this universe.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:17.590
I don't quite get what you're saying, but it doesn't matter, right?

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:18.900
Yeah, no problem!

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:21.410
O–Okay!

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:27.830
Oh, Mako-chan!

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:28.360
Hello...

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:33.690
Mako-chan, are you a middle school student?

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.450
You're not an elementary school student, right?

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:39.970
Y-Yes.

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:42.270
Why are you speaking so politely?

00:12:42.270 --> 00:12:46.650
Because I'm just an insignificant person.

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:49.600
You address yourself as 'ore' even though you're a girl.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:52.400
That's just the way I am.

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:54.860
Why are you sweating so much, Mako-chan?

00:12:54.860 --> 00:13:00.760
It's because the summer sun is shining on me.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.560
But it's winter right now.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:03.690
You're right.

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:06.410
She's probably figured it out!

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.530
You're being pretty quiet today, Mako-chan.

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:09.740
It seems like Yoshino is interested in Mako-chan.
You're being pretty quiet today, Mako-chan.

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:11.710
It seems like Yoshino is interested in Mako-chan.

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:33.450
She's looking at me.

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:39.010
Yo! You guys are doing homework, right? Count me in.

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:40.210
Sure.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:41.890
Eh? Where's Uchida?

00:13:41.890 --> 00:13:44.000
She went out to buy some things with Shuuichi-kun.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:45.410
Touma!

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:47.190
What is it?

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:51.000
I'm begging you, please sit between Yoshino and me to obstruct her attacks!

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:52.920
Why? What happened?

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:55.280
She's been staring at me for a while now!

00:13:56.480 --> 00:14:00.270
As expected from the "attentively sharp" Miss Yoshino.

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:02.720
Perhaps she's already suspicious of you.

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:04.700
Who referred to her as such?

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:05.960
Chiaki did.

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:13.080
Listen, rather than thinking about being exposed or not, worry about not getting thrown off by your enemy.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.810
This is your fight.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:16.190
I–Is that so?

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:18.440
Good luck then.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:20.100
Wait! Where're you going?

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:26.860
The homework that your class got today might turn out to be the homework for my class tomorrow.

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:30.080
I'll finish it before it's given. This is my fight.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:36.660
That's why the spot between Chiaki and Yoshino would be advantageous in gaining support from both sides.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:40.180
I'm begging you! Please stay here!

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:41.830
Shut up!

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:46.880
Hey, stop making a ruckus!

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:51.850
Why is Mako-chan panicking so much?

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.690
Even though we're both girls.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:56.510
You're so weird, Mako-chan!

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:01.740
I'm going home!

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.880
That's it. I can't take it anymore.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:13.870
Maybe it's about time I stop.

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:15.240
What's wrong with that?

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.450
Oh, it's you Kana.

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:19.720
What should I do?

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:22.000
One will grow to love the rice cakes she once hated.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.880
I–I do like rice cakes.

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:29.540
Well, do whatever you want. You won't be able to enter my place without those clothes though.

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:33.850
I'm done.

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:37.410
It's so much quicker when you put great minds together.

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:39.730
I think it's due to the absence of idiots.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.660
That one already went home early.

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:44.910
Umm...

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:46.160
What?

00:15:46.810 --> 00:15:49.790
I have something to ask of you, Chiaki.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:53.790
I want to change too, just like you have.

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:55.150
What are you saying suddenly?

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:58.240
I hate plain yogurt!

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:03.030
I hate carrots.

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:04.000
That's not it!

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:13.050
I have to buy groceries...

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:18.110
Have I changed?

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:19.900
I feel that you have.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.180
In what way?

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:24.100
You talk more often now.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:27.040
I don't think I've changed though.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:31.320
Besides, I don't think a nickname alone would change a person.

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:33.280
Yeah.

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:36.860
Don't look so down. It's something you have to figure out yourself.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:40.640
You have your good points too, Shuuichi-kun.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:40.990
Teddy launches!

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:42.380
Eh? Such as?
Teddy launches!

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:44.850
Well, if you ask me...

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:47.960
If I had to say, then you're...

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:50.140
Then I'm...

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:50.960
You're not an idiot at least.

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:55.070
Don't worry too much. You're pretty smart, right?

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:57.470
Y–You're right.

00:16:57.710 --> 00:17:00.890
Or are you saying that attaching idiot to your identity is better?

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:01.450
Fly teddy!
Or are you saying that attaching idiot to your identity is better?

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:01.680
Fly teddy!

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.980
N-No.
Fly teddy!

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:13.580
Hey!

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:15.110
What is it?

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:16.960
You're just going to ignore your sister beside you?

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:18.770
There's only 100 million yen.

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:20.750
Not that, listen.

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:23.410
I dreamt of you munching on carrot sticks.

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:24.630
Huh?

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:27.610
And it looked as though you were eating something delicious.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.420
Look! Coincidentally these are the carrot sticks that I saw in my dream!

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.470
Get out of my sight!

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:36.540
Now Chiaki, eat up.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:37.630
No friggin chance!

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:41.430
If this doesn't become reality, then we might not have supper!

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:43.300
What're you doing?

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:44.640
I'm home.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:54.240
Chiaki, I'm leaving your change of clothes here!

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:55.860
Yes, Haruka-neesama.

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:59.140
Haruka-neesama. Umm...

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.290
What is it?

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:02.720
Have I changed?

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.070
Why do you say that all of a sudden?

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:08.130
Today, someone told me that I've changed.

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:09.550
Your friend did?

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:10.320
Yes.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.340
Then most likely you have.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:18.120
You get influenced by the people around you without realizing it.

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.350
Come have dinner after you finish your bath.

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:27.660
I got it right!

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.390
Who cares?

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:32.040
For crabs, first the shell!

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.700
Right! The shell...

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:43.350
I see. So I made a mistake.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:47.750
I thought they were carrot sticks, but they were actually crab legs.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:50.750
But I guess there's no point in saying that now.

00:18:54.740 --> 00:18:57.930
Because crabs are meant to be eaten quietly.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.570
Morning!

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:07.860
Good morning!

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:09.880
Good morning. What's wrong?

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.930
What is it, you ask?

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.580
Your whipped cream!

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:16.360
Whipped cream? One of your prophetic dreams again?

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:18.210
You probably didn't dream of anything anyway.

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:20.380
I did... but I forgot!

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:24.080
What should we do?

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:24.910
About what?

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:26.440
About Chiaki! Chiaki!

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:28.660
Is this a joke?

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:31.710
I... didn't see anything.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:33.940
You're letting it slide, aren't you?

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:37.880
I don't know how long it'll stay that way though. I got it.

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:42.220
What are you muttering about over there?

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:47.960
Good morning.

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:49.010
Good morning?

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:50.430
Good morning!

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.190
What's the matter?

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:55.130
N–Nothing.

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:57.820
Did you bring your homework?

00:19:57.830 --> 00:19:58.910
Homework?

00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:00.110
Speaking of homework...

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:04.610
Mako-chan! I wonder what she's doing now.

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:06.330
Minami-ke.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:07.110
Okawari!

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:11.650
Tighten your necktie properly, Hosaka.

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:12.960
Yes, sensei.

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:17.340
Yay! Haruka-chan made me a bento!

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:22.420
Why did you hit me?

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:24.010
Why did you try to steal it?

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:31.140
Hosaka, you made bentos every day hoping that Haruka would eat it, right?

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:33.060
Even though you've never given them to her.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:36.330
Do you want to eat this bento made by Haruka?

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:39.090
Or would you rather have Haruka eat your bento?

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:40.520
Which one?

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:44.410
Hayami-senpai! About today's club activities–

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:46.560
Maki! I'm asking for your opinion as a strategist.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:49.980
Am I to eat? Or am I to be eaten?

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:51.020
Answer me!

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:53.590
I think you should be doing the eating.

00:20:54.010 --> 00:20:55.130
I see.

00:20:56.580 --> 00:21:00.000
Maki! Don't just go spouting nonsense just so you can escape!

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.750
It's because he's too disgusting... no, too intimidating, that's why.

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:06.450
The way you are now looks horrible.

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:10.510
Hosaka! You're a man that strives for the best in everything!

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:13.640
But right now, you have lost sight of your own self.

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:20.240
Think about it. What is it that you truly want? Who are you exactly?

00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:22.780
What... I truly want?

00:21:23.350 --> 00:21:25.850
Sensei, just what should I do?

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:27.440
Tighten your necktie properly.

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:28.370
Yes, sensei!

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:35.810
It's all your fault that my bento is messed up!
How are you going to make up for it?

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:38.350
You just kicked me.

00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:39.960
So what if I did?

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.290
Kick...

00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:44.670
I see, so this is the answer.

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:47.310
Be kicked or be slapped.

00:21:47.310 --> 00:21:48.980
To eat or to be eaten.

00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:51.830
It's not a matter of choosing between the two.

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:53.990
It's delicious either way!

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:55.720
That's right! For I'm Hosaka!

00:21:56.270 --> 00:21:58.830
Even if it's all messed up.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:21:59.900
I won't let you have it.

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:34.150
Are there people out there who think that drinking vinegar will soften their body?

00:23:34.150 --> 00:23:36.970
It's true that a fish's bones would soften by marinating it in vinegar.

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.380
But human bones and fish bones are different.

00:23:39.380 --> 00:23:42.630
Vinegar that gets absorbed into the body breaks down into carbon dioxide and water.

00:23:42.630 --> 00:23:44.920
It's better to give up now and do stretching exercises instead.
